help_lines('pin-item', [
"orbit-kb --dir PROJECT pin-item ID SOURCE --text-file F --changed-at T [--kind tracker|file] [--hub DIR] [--session S]",
"",
"Record a pin of a tracker item in a project KB, from item text that you pasted or exported",
"into the file F. orbit-kb computes the digest (sha256 of F). You give the change time",
"(--changed-at, UTC, such as 2026-10-01T09:00:00Z). --kind defaults to tracker.",
"It writes pin/5, so it takes the writer lock and accepts --take (D23). A pin id that exists",
"is rejected (exit 1). Nothing is fetched: no command uses a network.",
"It keeps the text of F as pins/HEX.txt in the KB (HEX of the digest; D27). orbit-kb show pin ID prints it.",
"A new pin can make a draft lose by date (lost_by_date). pin-item then records each new drop in",
"the hub ledger itself, once, as project dropped does (T45): the hub is --hub DIR, else the parent",
"of the KB when it has flow/flow.db; the session is --session S, else HUB_SESSION. It prints the",
"item id on stderr. The item is escalated: only a human closes it. With no hub, or when the ledger",
"does not take it, it prints one line that names the drop and the project dropped command to run.",
"A push over a newer tracker edit (pushed_over, T46) is recorded too: a note on the open item of",
"the drop, else one new item. A pane gets HUB_SESSION where it is started (orbit-kb help project).",
"The exit code is that of the pin."
]).
